 BY-SA 2.5","body":"superb post! Excellent."},{"owner":{"account_id":49918,"reputation":623,"user_id":1345,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/bbcfd46f9847b5a252bb06a88ccef8fd?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"kowsheek","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1345/kowsheek"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1289761508,"post_id":14753,"comment_id":28428,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I will agree, reading it helped me realize a lot about what we do and how to go about it."},{"owner":{"account_id":62820,"reputation":661,"user_id":12404,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/e02c3a863e8a241a674b29573f577563?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Matt Phillips","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/12404/matt-phillips"},"edited":false,"score":5,"creation_date":1289598780,"post_id":14771,"comment_id":28039,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"It means when you overthink a problem you can end up with horribly complex solutions that end up getting more complicated due to the previous design choices. To summarize the article linked they try to create a ridiculous body heating system to keep your hands warm. Instead of just wearing gloves"},{"owner":{"account_id":101797,"reputation":1251,"user_id":6518,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":100,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/297999f76faca5a6b28a1b83c815b232?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"jellyfishtree","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/6518/jellyfishtree"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1289598713,"post_id":14662,"comment_id":28037,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I hoped more people would upvote this. This book is amazing! It&#39;s not so much a guide for programming technique as it is strategy; showing you how to approach your programming career (and the profession of programming in general) by thinking of it as a life-long path and viewing yourself as an aspiring craftsman of a skilled art."},{"owner":{"account_id":38381,"reputation":1249,"user_id":5933,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7d631793919f6ce68944e5326da443ca?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"mlvljr","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/5933/mlvljr"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":6161,"reputation":16801,"user_id":1254,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/cbdd9440fc59edcde4faf1b84058fd2f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Frank Shearar","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1254/frank-shearar"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1289590726,"post_id":14652,"comment_id":27985,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"@Frank Shearar The guy just perefers simplicity to potential spaghetti I think. He also gave a lecture in Russian about a year ago; there he said that he prefers simple things like &quot;for, if&quot; and essentially sees nothing bad in writing Pascal in any language, if the code is effective and clear (as opposed to mistically duct-typed, as I get it)."},{"owner":{"account_id":87093,"reputation":10505,"user_id":6390,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/0e136cf9c453e09ad04424fae622ca93?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Ross Patterson","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/6390/ross-patterson"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1289582923,"post_id":18507,"comment_id":27916,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Tracy Kidder&#39;s <i>Soul of a New Machine</i> should be required reading for every professional programmer.  I&#39;ve given copies to every newly-minted wannabe-developer I&#39;ve mentored over the years.  Just understanding his concept of &quot;signing up&quot; is worth the price and time."},{"owner":{"account_id":42956,"reputation":1626,"user_id":2624,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7472e119fb9da9e90e84247da2c605bf?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Jonathan Sterling","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/2624/jonathan-sterling"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1289579501,"post_id":14692,"comment_id":27881,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I wanna be a rockstar developer like I wanna be a douchebag."},{"owner":{"account_id":20351,"reputation":28160,"user_id":1554,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/ebc680455d447f57613154ffd1946b9f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Steven Evers","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1554/steven-evers"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1289508679,"post_id":14693,"comment_id":27543,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"+1 for the gates/jobs interview. Great interview and totally correct on the hosts vs. guests note."},{"owner":{"account_id":20351,"reputation":28160,"user_id":1554,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/ebc680455d447f57613154ffd1946b9f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Steven Evers","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1554/steven-evers"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":89326,"reputation":1056,"user_id":7038,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/0af674d852c6671c1a4f3e75e686fb6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"kirk.burleson","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/7038/kirk-burleson"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1289508523,"post_id":14753,"comment_id":27542,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"@kirk.burleson: It still is."},{"owner":{"account_id":12145,"reputation":12915,"user_id":2429,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/NeuGc.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Mike Dunlavey","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/2429/mike-dunlavey"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1289503540,"post_id":14667,"comment_id":27501,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I shared an office with Richard at MIT back around 74-ish."},{"owner":{"account_id":5714,"reputation":4652,"user_id":89,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/a17a7b2048799c3d2c2f9aa4f8ec97c8?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Peter Boughton","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/89/peter-boughton"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1289163687,"post_id":14771,"comment_id":25800,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Kirk, you need to read the linked article for the answer to possibly make sense... though even then it doesn&#39;t really."},{"owner":{"account_id":89326,"reputation":1056,"user_id":7038,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/0af674d852c6671c1a4f3e75e686fb6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"kirk.burleson","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/7038/kirk-burleson"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1289147645,"post_id":14692,"comment_id":25742,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"He&#39;s a good writer and I love to read his stuff.  Just take some of it with a grain of salt or you may get depressed if you&#39;re not a rockstar developer."},{"owner":{"account_id":89326,"reputation":1056,"user_id":7038,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/0af674d852c6671c1a4f3e75e686fb6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"kirk.burleson","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/7038/kirk-burleson"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1289147474,"post_id":14771,"comment_id":25741,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I don&#39;t get it."},{"owner":{"account_id":89326,"reputation":1056,"user_id":7038,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/0af674d852c6671c1a4f3e75e686fb6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"kirk.burleson","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/7038/kirk-burleson"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1289147432,"post_id":14753,"comment_id":25740,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"It used to be a &quot;must read.&quot;"},{"owner":{"account_id":88744,"reputation":2028,"user_id":1668,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":100,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/d73c2bc38fa5906ce4e1d8fe16f0b1df?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Jonn","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1668/jonn"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1288092409,"post_id":14652,"comment_id":21153,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Is there some other source of this aside from the transcript? He noted that the transcript had mistranslations."},{"owner":{"account_id":6161,"reputation":16801,"user_id":1254,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/cbdd9440fc59edcde4faf1b84058fd2f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Frank Shearar","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1254/frank-shearar"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1288085870,"post_id":14652,"comment_id":21104,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"His comments on OOP are just plain wrong: <a href=\"http://www.stlport.org/resources/StepanovUSA.html\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">stlport.org/resources/StepanovUSA.html</a> He thinks OOP is single-dispatch and class-based, for starters. (CLOS uses multiple dispatch, Self and Javascript are prototype-based, as counterexamples.)"},{"owner":{"account_id":35904,"reputation":3961,"user_id":672,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/841f30e87e7dc3f9976edc846ae403b2?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Geek","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/672/geek"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":6161,"reputation":16801,"user_id":1254,"user_